<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zarbienus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zarbienus was a king of Gordyene (Corduene), in the mountains south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>, in the 1st century BCE, while it was subject to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigranes-the-great">Tigranes the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a>, he negotiated secretly with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> under Lucullus, was betrayed and put to death with his family by Tigranes. After invading Gordyene, Lucullus gave him a royal funeral and raised a monument in his honour.</p></div>
